Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:35:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(web): bound LAN pairing guesses with a process-wide
 budget

A per-peer lockout alone leaves the six-digit PIN guessable by a peer set that
rotates source addresses: five attempts per five minutes per address, and a
local process has all of 127/8 to spend. `maxTotalFailedAttempts` (default 50)
counts failed submissions across every peer and stops pairing once the budget
is spent, so the guesses available against one process PIN are bounded however
many addresses the attacker uses. Only a restart reopens pairing, which the 429
body names.

The budget is keyed by the root application context like the PIN, so a
Connection hot reload cannot hand an attacker a fresh budget for a PIN the
operator already read.
